"""Build the versioned stage instruction resources; no story content is generated."""
from pathlib import Path
import os
if os.getenv('ODD_EPISODE_WORKER')=='1':raise SystemExit('Shared prompt generation is a development-only operation')

ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
STAGES={
'01_IDEA_GENERATION':('Story Developer', '''INPUT: confirmed category and primary genre, optional secondary genre, and prior concepts. OUTPUT: exactly five complete v2 concepts matching the supplied schema. Use its precise field names and include all ten concise editorial assessments. Explicit legacy_general v1 requests retain their ten-idea schema and original field names. No script or downstream package at this stage.

Explore genuinely different emotional experiences, casts, locations, conflicts and ending types. Favor unusual but understandable events, meaningful choices and causal payoffs. Do not reskin the same betrayal/karma premise. Animals, stickmen and original fantasy creatures all share the Midnight Gold design system. Explain feasibility through simple visible poses, manageable prop exchanges and coherent scene geography. Do not require a fixed image count.

Internally evaluate hook comprehension, character desire, middle developments, fair payoff, originality relative to supplied history, sharing motivation and visual feasibility. Repair weak candidates before returning them. An editorial judgment is not a viral prediction. Do not claim exhaustive originality screening or invent audience preferences. Wait for the user's story selection.'''),
'02_SCRIPT_WRITING':('Story Developer', '''INPUT: selected idea or explicit custom premise, optional draft and recent story context. OUTPUT: JSON matching Script schema: exact narration-only text, story brief, actionable findings. Use one narrator, natural American English, complete causal story, default 45–75 second creative target. No stage directions, timing codes or Markdown in narration.

Start with a meaningful event and specific question. By five seconds communicate who/what matters and stakes. Select a suitable structure rather than a mandatory flash-forward. Give characters desires, agency and consequences. Deliver developments and small rewards throughout. A mystery's reveal should be supported by clues; fantasy has comprehensible rules; horror has stakes; comedy has setup and payoff. No forced lesson, twist, happy ending or follow request. Do not pad.

Internally critique and improve opening, clarity, progression, emotion, visual producibility, originality and ending before returning. The next review task may improve this unapproved draft. Timings remain estimates until actual audio exists. Do not generate characters, storyboard or image jobs yet. Preserve a supplied approved script if the task is downstream; script revision only occurs before approval or after explicit revocation.'''),
'03_SCRIPT_REVIEW':('Retention Editor', '''INPUT: selected concept plus complete unapproved draft. OUTPUT: same Script schema with the final improved narration, coherent brief and concrete review findings. This is internal review before the single approval boundary. Do not ask the owner to approve another artifact.

Cold-read the first line: identify the event, stakes and exact curiosity question. Find filler, repeated emotion, unexplained objects, ambiguous geography, implausible choices, predictable or unearned payoffs and missing causal transitions. Audit meaningful developments and micro-payoffs. Check for disguised copied plots against the actual supplied history, labeling limitations. Choose the three most valuable fixes and implement them in the returned unapproved narration; findings explain what changed and why.

Keep the selected genre and emotional promise. Do not automatically impose advice, twist, happy ending, horror staging or recurring hero. Prefer clear still-image scenes over impossible crowded choreography. Evaluate attention, curiosity, emotion, middle progression, visual clarity, micro-payoffs, ending, sharing, originality and brand consistency. Explain qualitative evidence; never output viral percentages or imply proven audience performance. After the owner approves, this task cannot run on the frozen script without revocation.'''),
'04_CHARACTER_BIBLE':('Continuity Supervisor + Visual Prompt Director', '''INPUT: immutable approved narration, idea, approval hash and Package JSON schema. OUTPUT: one COMPLETE Package JSON, coordinating this stage with 05_STORYBOARD, 06_FLOW_IMAGE_PROMPTS, 07_RETENTION_AUDIT and 11_PUBLISHING instructions supplied in task input. Never output a revised narration. Each scene's narration_text must partition the approved script in its original order, covering every word exactly once. Joining scene spans with spaces must reproduce its normalized text.

Create story-specific original characters with unique C001-style IDs, names, desire and complete descriptions (species/stickman identity, proportions, face, fur/colors, outfit, anatomy, distinguishing markers, allowable expressions and props). No generic reused cast or undefined costumes. The continuity_matrix locks location geography, entrances, time/weather/light, prop inventory and state transitions, wardrobe, relationships and chronology. Distinguish initial state from consequences. Preserve exact character identity across each relevant scene; scene character_ids may only refer to this package's cast.

Provide complete scene-specific visible beats, locations, prop state/counts, expression/pose, first-look target/reason, precise meaningful gold placement, physical lighting, framing, continuity and normalized protected_regions for faces/clues. Choose a stable caption_y (.2–.7) whose two-line caption box avoids these regions. Use enough scenes for meaningful new information, not a rigid quota. All illustrations are static and never move. For every scene also author the editorial plan for the boundary INTO that scene: transition_in (exactly one of hard_cut, short_crossfade, emotional_crossfade, dip_to_charcoal, graphic_match_cut; S001 is always hard_cut) and a short transition_reason naming the narrative purpose, as described in 05_STORYBOARD, caption_style (default or soft_fade for quiet moments) and emphasis_phrase (empty, or 1-4 consecutive words copied exactly from that scene's narration_text for the single most important spoken reveal). Provide ten explainable retention criteria, instrumental direction and publishing draft. Required fields must contain actual story content; no TODO/TBD, unresolved brackets or placeholders. Contradictions must fail clearly rather than inventing a different story.'''),
'05_STORYBOARD':('Continuity Supervisor', '''INPUT: approved script, character definitions and continuity. OUTPUT: scenes within Package schema. Assign consecutive stable S001-style IDs. narration_text spans partition the entire approved narration in order. A still must add action, reaction, clue, choice, obstacle, consequence, revelation or emotional development. Do not display a later outcome under earlier narration.

For each scene specify exact visible beat; cast IDs; full location and layout; props/counts/open/closed/damage states; expression and pose; primary target and story function; yellow surface and material versus emissive mechanism; real light source/direction; camera angle and portrait composition; continuity locks; normalized protected face/clue regions and caption-safe center position. Essential details should remain legible at mobile thumbnail size. No text is generated within artwork.

Before audio, calculate only provisional duration/coverage estimates. Do not claim exact spoken-word timestamps. After audio, preserve scene IDs and assets while grounding cuts in supplied subtitle cue boundaries; if a scene boundary lies inside an unaligned cue, require genuine corrected cue timing rather than distributing words evenly. Do not invent new events to fill time. No generated moving clips, image zoom/pan/parallax or animated character cutouts.

TRANSITIONS (ODD_FRAME_CINEMATIC_TRANSITIONS_V1): the stills stay completely static; only the boundary between two stills may be styled, and every transition is silent. For every scene choose transition_in, the transition FROM the previous still INTO this one, as an editor would, from exactly five names. hard_cut (the default, zero frames): visual hooks, sudden discoveries, reactions, changes of action, important beats, suspense, revelations and fast progression; it must feel intentional. graphic_match_cut (zero frames): only when the two neighbouring compositions are deliberately designed to correspond (same shape, position or framing, e.g. a round golden clock to a round golden eye); describe the match in both scenes' framing so the illustrations actually deliver it. short_crossfade (about 7 frames): gentle emotional continuity, quiet moments, friendship, sadness, romance, subtle atmospheric change; avoid it where two character silhouettes would overlap confusingly. emotional_crossfade (about 11 frames, sparingly): important emotional pauses, memories, reflection and gentle resolutions, never inside fast suspense or action. dip_to_charcoal (about 12 frames to #14171C and back, sparingly): meaningful time jumps, major location or chapter changes and dramatic separations, never an ordinary scene change. Explain the narrative purpose in transition_reason. S001 is always hard_cut. As a loose guide roughly 65% hard or graphic match cuts, 25% short crossfades and 10% dips or emotional crossfades, but these are not quotas: a tense mystery may be almost all hard cuts. Never choose at random, never transition every boundary, no wipes, slides, glitches, zooms or spins, and never invent other names: unknown names are rejected. Durations come from the pinned profile; transitions overlap existing scene boundaries and never change narration timing, caption timing or the total duration. Also mark at most one emphasis_phrase per scene (1-4 consecutive words from that scene's narration_text) for the key reveal, or leave it empty.'''),
'06_FLOW_IMAGE_PROMPTS':('Visual Prompt Director', '''INPUT: approved Package, exact character descriptors and scene locks. OUTPUT: deterministic Queue Studio JSON compiled by backend from these fields; schema_version, episode_id and jobs ONLY. Jobs have job_id S001_IMG, scene_id S001, type image, full prompt, source_image null and output_name S001. No extra top-level keys or video jobs.

Each prompt must stand alone, repeating the entire relevant character descriptions and states. Include exact scene context and visible story beat; proportions/species/anatomy; expressions/poses; approved props/counts; detailed environmental layout; portrait 9:16 framing; target and why it matters; exact #FFD43B placement; quiet charcoal/slate background; ivory readable features; motivated source/direction of light; matte gold never emitting light; ink contours, flat colors, stepped shading and restrained texture; continuity restrictions. Genre controls mood without breaking Midnight Gold hierarchy.

Explicitly exclude photorealism, 3D/CGI, realistic human faces, inconsistent identities, extra limbs, text, logos and watermarks. Never request movement or imply image generation occurred because a prompt exists. Validate unique IDs and full storyboard coverage. Batch exports preserve the same schema and original IDs; never regenerate completed assets automatically.'''),
'07_RETENTION_AUDIT':('Retention Editor', '''INPUT: approved script and provisional storyboard; optionally actual completed timeline and QC. OUTPUT: exactly ten Package retention entries with criterion, rating (strong/adequate/revise), concrete evidence and actionable recommendation. Criteria: Opening attention, Curiosity, Emotional stakes, Mid-story progression, Visual comprehensibility, Micro-payoffs, Ending satisfaction, Shareability, Originality, Brand consistency.

Describe the specific first-three-second event and central question, understandable character desire, causal developments, visual variety, earned payoff, fresh concept, Midnight Gold recognition, authentic reason to share and reason to return. State whether evidence is script-only, provisional storyboard or measured edit. Distinguish creative assumptions from verified scientific findings and actual audience data. Do not fabricate retention curves, viral odds or quantitative audience predictions.

Before approval, improve weak drafts internally. After approval, audit rather than rewriting. Critical contradictions block affected work; uncertain judgments become warnings. A technical export check cannot prove a narrative is emotionally satisfying. Completed edit audits include actual scene/caption coverage and known timing limitations; human review and listening remain useful.'''),
'08_REMOTION_EDIT':('Timeline Editor + Typography Director', '''INPUT: approved script hash, validated stills, actual narration duration, SRT cues or genuine alignment, storyboard scene spans and protected_regions. OUTPUT: timeline.json plus captions.json using measured cue evidence. Caption and shot boundaries must be narration-grounded. Do not derive fake word timestamps by equal division of a long SRT cue.

STATIC illustrations only, full portrait frame without stretching. No image transforms, zoom/pan, parallax, character animation, generated video or effects layers on the artwork. Scene boundaries use one validated decision per boundary (from_scene, to_scene, transition, duration_frames, narrative_reason) taken from the episode's transition decisions file, otherwise the storyboard's transition_in, otherwise the deterministic fallback, always limited by the pinned editing profile: hard cut, graphic match cut, short crossfade (5-8 frames), emotional crossfade (9-12) or dip to charcoal (10-14). Use the official @remotion/transitions TransitionSeries with the shared crossfade() and dipToCharcoal() presentations; give each still half of each neighbouring transition as a handle so the midpoint of every transition sits on the narration-grounded boundary, the series is exactly the narration length and no caption is shifted. Captions are a continuous layer above the stills and never restart at a scene change. Transitions are data, never generated code. Ensure no gaps/overlaps, no ending reveal early and no conclusion illustration under prior narration. If supplied SRT crosses scene boundaries or has more than four words per cue without alignment, show actionable correction requirements.

Required centered captions: Barlow Condensed ExtraBold 800; white, strong black outline, subtle shadow; max two lines, 1–4 words per synchronized phrase, scene-stable location near .46 height unless face/clue regions require relocation. Load licensed font files. Classic v1.0 uses Quick Pop (scales .94→1 over 4–6 frames with a fast fade then a stable hold). Cinematic Flow v1.1 (default for new episodes) uses Wave Reveal (staggered letters rise with a smooth wave over 5–8 frames, then stay perfectly still), Smooth Phrase Replace for continuous phrases, Glow Pop with restrained golden-yellow emphasis for the key reveal, Immediate Impact when narration is fast and Soft Fade for quiet moments. Fill stays white with a thick black outline and a soft white glow that rises briefly as a phrase lands and then settles; no constant pulsing or blur. Only text animates. No caption before its speech cue. Export frame-based deterministic composition at 1080×1920 30 FPS. Exactly narration plus instrumental sources.'''),
'09_AUDIO_MIXING':('Audio Mixing Director', '''INPUT: actual narration and user-supplied instrumental; user rights evidence; measured loudness and durations. OUTPUT: audio_mix.json reporting source paths/hashes, measurements, gain, ducking, fades, final loudness/true peak and warnings. Do not invent a music file or its license.

Exactly TWO intended source tracks. Narration foreground and instrumental background ONLY. No SFX, ambience, whooshes, notifications, impacts, vocal music or extra dialogue. Measure both sources with FFmpeg loudness analysis. Start music approximately 21 dB below speech integrated level (18–24 dB guide), then sidechain smooth ducking, avoid pumping, fade boundaries and limit true peaks. Use two-pass loudnorm where feasible. Confirm no clipping and actual duration.

Missing rights evidence is reported, not represented as licensed. Automated signal measurements cannot prove the music is instrumental or artistically appropriate; record the user's declaration and listening limitation. Simulated phone mono/bandpass and headphones review are useful but do not invent listening results. Preserve unmodified originals and reproducible processing settings. The Remotion composition may consume the two normalized tracks or a verified two-source mix, never an SFX bus.'''),
'10_QC_AND_EXPORT':('QA Agent', '''INPUT: frozen approval and export authorization, asset fingerprints, assembled timeline, actual preview and encoded final media. OUTPUT: machine-readable QC plus QC_REPORT.md distinguishing executed checks, blockers, warnings and human-benefit checks.

Fail on revoked/mismatched narration approval, missing/corrupt assets, ungrounded scene boundaries, caption text mismatch, image aspect mismatch, missing font, wrong soundtrack sources, stale asset fingerprints, decode failure or incorrect video settings. Verify scene order and coverage, required captions within safe bounds, no image-motion code path, no AI video inputs or SFX, measured audio levels, no clipping and complete audio/video duration. FFprobe must verify actual h264 1080×1920 30 FPS and AAC; fully decode the output and test for blank frames.

Render a review preview first, validate it, then automatically export final when gates pass under the single script authorization. No second creative approval. Do not publish. Preserve editable Remotion props and manifests, progress, history and failed-job logs. Never label quality perfect based on metadata checks; actual visual storytelling, illustration fidelity, instrumental content and listening benefit from human viewing. Retry is idempotent and must not rewrite scripts or replace approved assets.'''),
'11_PUBLISHING':('Creative Director', '''INPUT: approved story, genre, payoff and measured duration if available. OUTPUT: concise Markdown publishing draft within Package: proposed title, honest caption, optional relevant keywords, cover-still recommendation and optional authentic discussion question. Fiction remains fiction. Do not spoil a reveal unnecessarily in public-facing copy; internal planning may discuss it.

No automatic Facebook upload, invented handle, Meta Insights access, guaranteed reach, monetization promise, fabricated rights or irrelevant hashtags. No forced subscribe request, moral lesson or engagement bait. Use natural American English and culturally portable stakes without claiming country-locked reach. Verify current platform policies before making specific factual claims; store supplied metrics with periods/definitions instead of manufacturing a predicted retention curve.

Record a proposed test hypothesis and available real measurement to use after publication. Explain why someone might share and return without claiming the hypothesis is established research. Preserve original approved story; recommendations for future Reels do not mutate it. Leave publication URL, dates and metrics empty until supplied.''')}

VERSIONS={'01_IDEA_GENERATION':'2.0.0','02_SCRIPT_WRITING':'2.0.0','03_SCRIPT_REVIEW':'2.0.0','04_CHARACTER_BIBLE':'1.3.0','05_STORYBOARD':'1.3.0','08_REMOTION_EDIT':'1.3.0'}
GENRE_MARKER='## Category-driven story identity (v2)'
master=(ROOT/'prompts/00_MASTER_PROMPT.md').read_text(encoding='utf-8')
if GENRE_MARKER not in master:raise SystemExit('The versioned master prompt must contain the category-driven contract')
genre_contract=GENRE_MARKER+master.split(GENRE_MARKER,1)[1]
ONLY=set(__import__('sys').argv[1:])
for name,(role,body) in STAGES.items():
    if ONLY and name not in ONLY:continue
    suffix='\n\n'+genre_contract if name in VERSIONS else ''
    (ROOT/'prompts'/f'{name}.md').write_text(f'# ODD FRAME — {name}\n\nVersion: {VERSIONS.get(name,"1.0.0")}\nResponsibility: {role}\n\nThis stage requires the mandatory four-document loader and master prompt. Latest ODD_FRAME_RULES.json overrides historical conflicts. Return only the requested format; never claim a failed model call succeeded.\n\n{body}\n{suffix}',encoding='utf-8')
print('Wrote eleven operational stage prompts.')
